      "Language": "chi",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": [
        {
          "NlmCategory": "OBJECTIVE",
          "Label": "OBJECTIVE",
          "content": "To evaluate the correlation between the gene polymorphism of IL-1beta-511 or IL-1RN VNTR and the risk of coronary heart disease (CHD)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "METHODS",
          "Label": "METHODS",
          "content": "The patient-control studies on the association of IL-1=-511 or IL-1RN VNTR gene polymorphism with the risk of CHD were searched according to the inclusion criteria. Heterogeneity tests were conducted for the data from each study before Meta-analysis."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "RESULTS",
          "Label": "RESULTS",
          "content": "For the 7 studies addressing the correlation between IL-1beta-511 polymorphism and the susceptibility of CHD, the pooled odds ratio was about 1.04 with 95% CI of 0.93-1.18 (Z=0.71, P=0.48). For the 5 studies of the correlation between IL-1RN VNTR polymorphism and the susceptibility of CHD, the pooled odds ratio was about 1.01 and the 95% CI was 0.78-1.17 (Z=0.08, P=0.93)."
        },
        {
          "NlmCategory": "CONCLUSIONS",
          "Label": "CONCLUSION",
          "content": "The gene polymorphism of IL-1beta-511 or IL-1RN VNTR has no correlation to the susceptibility of CHD, but is associated with in the disease development and clinical phenotype."
        }
      ]},
